9921c","position":{"commit_sha":"1a07762988d6d10e6f2195ddff6c4e471fdeb1b3","position":"1793223646022669100-61379625-22c0-429e-ad57-735499c9921c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"66d490a7dac8ab13b096a7a7339e6d00a153eeea8c38ae92d08a9365d4c49010","event_uuid":"75263a9c-3f5e-45d4-b2e3-4e0097daa292","position":{"commit_sha":"325bf0b761f1911a8977af96ddaa5405d84c3834","position":"1793224677128829665-75263a9c-3f5e-45d4-b2e3-4e0097daa292"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"e9d317bc986a832f8fc833a71a442592a6d28170fa27556d26fa28ca1686ce4c","event_uuid":"644b335e-4a4c-444e-9926-230fdcefd067","position":{"commit_sha":"5124de0953d209c85dcdedcc1fe455033ed16a24","position":"1793224685366449709-644b335e-4a4c-444e-9926-230fdcefd067"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision recorded 2026-10-27 (operator): ship an idempotent ensure-registry migration (docs/migrations.md) that selects tickets whose SNAPSHOT carries force_close_reason with last_reopened_at set (or force_close_reason on a non-closed status) and rebuilds them with rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log. It runs on the first write after the change merges.","timestamp":1793146910342070312},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision (operator): ship the snapshot-close-metadata ensure unit with its cost documented, then run `rebar store fsck --repair` once after the change merges. Dry run on a remote-less copy of the 300,866-commit tracker: the first sweep rebuilt the 12 stale SNAPSHOTs in 1,482.6 s under the write lock and made 12 commits; the second sweep took 21.5 s and made 0 commits (ok, no unconverged tickets). Of the first sweep, about 7.4 min was the per-ticket commit-map lookup; the remaining ~17 min is unprofiled. Unchecked: null commit shas in the rebuilt ledgers, and how long a blocked writer waits before failing. State: committed on branch fix-df72-stale-snapshot-close (rebased on origin/main 2fb6062bfe5); 7 new unit tests pass; make check passes; make verify running before the Gerrit push.","timestamp":1793211599407941694},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit change 3127 merged (3835269d792) with the snapshot-close-metadata ensure unit. Live repair run with `rebar store fsck --repair` on 2026-10-28, 14:00:22 to 14:33:03 PDT (32 min 41 s wall). Ensure sweep: rebuilt all 12 stale SNAPSHOTs (075b, 14f4, 40a7, 52b0, 7332, 76b2, 84e6, 858c, a881, a8ea, ad81, e215), 30 to 74 s each, about 10.5 min in total; `ensures: 10/10 applied`. The a3 remediation committed batch 1 (313 files) and then aborted because its push was rejected as non-fast-forward (origin had moved); the remaining batches did not run, and fsck issues went from 102 to 30. Re-run `rebar store fsck --repair` to finish the remediation. Earlier measurements in this ticket came from a dry run through a cp -R copy of .tickets-tracker; that copy's .git file points at the live gitdir, so those 12 rebuilds, and a `git remote remove` run through the copy, hit the live tracker repo (local rebuild commits were rolled back to origin before this repair). Boot-time sweeps (op-cert workspace, MCP boot) also run this unit; on an unconverged origin each costs the rebuild time, and on a converged one about 21.5 s per sweep.","timestamp":1793223294460109564},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local tracker clone integrated with origin: the 12 REBUILD SNAPSHOT commits and a3-remediation batch 1 from the 14:00 PDT repair are now pushed. The a3 remediation stays incomplete (batch 1 only); re-run rebar store fsck --repair to finish it.","timestamp":1793223350071448001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1792361518962037693,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"67417562-f814-48e1-90b7-c31c16519881","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"6df4-d3f0-a447-4ba3"},{"link_uuid":"cb66688b-0c34-455a-bb3a-880c7b37c73c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1279-c7cd-aea5-4432"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`process_snapshot` (`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py`) copies every key of a SNAPSHOT's\n`compiled_state` into reduced state, and ordinary replay starts at the latest SNAPSHOT.\nAny ticket compacted after a forced close was followed by reopen (bug 6df4-d3f0, fixed in\nthe reducer fold) has the stale `force_close_reason` / `close_class` / `close_reason` /\n`completion_expectation` frozen into its SNAPSHOT. Fixing the fold and bumping the reducer\ncache version does not reach these: replay never re-folds the retired source events.\n\n## Evidence (this repo's tracker, 2026-10-18)\n\n- 8 SNAPSHOTs with `status: closed`, a `force_close_reason`, and `last_reopened_at` set,\n  whose most recent closing STATUS event carried no force reason (e.g. aabf-d89e,\n  a8ea-be28, ad81-73ad, 3d7a-7795, 7332-a728, a881-2d9a, 52b0-6a6a, 14f4-d616).\n- 4 SNAPSHOTs with status open/in_progress still carrying `force_close_reason`\n  (76b2-4b5f, 075b-1479, 84e6-0fda, e215-ab23).\n\n## Approach to decide in plan review\n\n`rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log` (`src/rebar/_commands/compact_rebuild.py`) already\nrecomputes a SNAPSHOT from the full log including `*.retired` sources, under the write\nlock with a crash-safe sentinel. A one-shot idempotent migration in the ensure-registry\n(`docs/migrations.md`) could select tickets whose SNAPSHOT carries `force_close_reason`\nand `last_reopened_at` and rebuild them. This mutates the shared tracker, so it is split\nfrom the pure reducer fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every SNAPSHOT whose compiled close metadata disagrees with a full-log reduction is\n  rebuilt; a fixture store with a stale closed SNAPSHOT reduces with no `force_close_reason`.\n- [x] The migration is idempotent (second run makes no writes).\n\n## Testing\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit -k snapshot_close_metadata -q\n```","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1279-c7cd-aea5-4432"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"75263a9c-3f5e-45d4-b2e3-4e0097daa292","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"df72-d570-8c77-44d4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Compacted SNAPSHOTs bake in stale force_close_reason from a pre-reopen forced close","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9a9f46f4-f279-47cc-b85a-84f03162b596","46b15b35-109a-40c7-8bba-a80a3f6cc066","e3c91f65-bac0-4596-8907-e3cca6db7d2e","205c61e6-fab5-45fa-88b4-368fb40eec1e","f0394090-76b4-4a7f-8fe3-35f9aa5ad828","cb66688b-0c34-455a-bb3a-880c7b37c73c","0922b541-d57e-462a-b760-ecb934979788","2e11cb67-93c2-4347-82d4-22fddfc227a8","61379625-22c0-429e-ad57-735499c9921c","86d58048-e5e3-4d20-9fae-94c916d17f4b","75263a9c-3f5e-45d4-b2e3-4e0097daa292","644b335e-4a4c-444e-9926-230fdcefd067"]},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1793227050050614660,"uuid":"10727448-bc03-4b32-8f23-31b